## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`options`): This is where the Contentstack SDK Stack is initialized. The options object (lines 55-67) configures only the delivery API (api_key, delivery_token, environment, branch) with no live_preview config. Contentstack's Live Preview requires a `live_preview` property in the Stack initialization options (with enable, host, preview_token). Without it, the SDK can only fetch published content — draft/preview content from the CMS is never served, making live preview impossible. Every downstream component (useContent → ContentstackProvider → all 236+ callers) only ever receives published content because this initialization site omits the preview configuration.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add a `live_preview` property to the `options` object, conditionally populated from new env vars (CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST, CONTENTSTACK_ENABLE_LIVE_PREVIEW). Destructure these alongside the existing env vars at lines 17-24. The live_preview block should be: `...(CONTENTSTACK_ENABLE_LIVE_PREVIEW === 'true' ? { live_preview: { enable: true, host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST, preview_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN } } : {})`. This is the Contentstack SDK's documented mechanism for enabling Live Preview — the Stack must be initialized with it; it cannot be added after `contentstack.Stack(options)` is called. The existing `isTestEnv` utility (already imported at line 6) can optionally guard the env-var validation, matching the pattern at lines 28-52.


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- Given a CMS editor has saved draft (unpublished) changes to a page's content in Contentstack, when they open that page via the CMS's Live Preview entry point, then the rendered page displays the draft content, including the unpublished changes.
- Given a headline exists only in draft form (never published) with the exact text "Preview Draft Headline", when the editor opens the page in Live Preview, then the text "Preview Draft Headline" is visibly rendered on the page.
- Given an editor is previewing a page with draft changes, when they make an additional edit in the CMS and refresh the preview, then the newly edited content is visible on the rendered page without the content having been published.
- Given Live Preview is opened on each of the GO, UP, and MX market sites, when a page with unpublished draft content is previewed on each site, then each site's rendered page displays its own market's draft content.
- Given a visitor opens a page normally (not via Live Preview), when the page renders, then it displays the currently published content with no draft or unpublished changes visible.
- Given Live Preview cannot be started (e.g., invalid or expired preview access), when the editor opens the page, then the page still renders its content normally with no blank screen or visible error state.

